{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DtNYtrqpBz1o5PLKq5bjX7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-535\"\n3\ttitle = \"Adjudicator telemetry first, dial off: session id and occupancy / window / percent per family; the stale grok slug\"\n4\tspecref = \"\"\n5\tworkstream = \"process\"\n6\tsr_refs = []\n7\tneeds = []\n8\tbuildtier = \"quick\"\n9\tsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\n10\tpriority = 2\n11\t+++\n12\t\n13\t## Deliverable\n14\t\n15\tTelemetry-first step of the adjudicator session-retention plan (plan §5 step\n16\t1), landed with the retention dial off — no mint, no resume argv, no session\n17\tstore, no `[adjudicator]` table (WI-540's job):\n18\t\n19\t- `project-trajectory/scripts/agent_loop.py`: new `family_context_telemetry(family, data)`\n20\t  reads session id and context occupancy/window/percent straight off the\n21\t  process's own JSON result, per family. ANTHROPIC's stream-json result\n22\t  already carries `session_id` on every call; occupancy sums the same four\n23\t  `usage` counters `session_meta` already partially reads\n24\t  (input + cache-read + cache-creation + output); window is picked only from\n25\t  the unique `modelUsage` entry whose own four counters match those same\n26\t  top-level totals, so a subagent with colliding input/output but different\n27\t  cache usage is never mistaken for the session — left blank when a full\n28\t  match is absent or ambiguous, per the plan's \"never guessed\" rule. OPENAI/OPENCODE\n29\t  return blank: their shipped one-shot templates carry no\n30\t  `--json`/`--format json`, so there is nothing to parse until WI-540's\n31\t  per-family adapter lands.\n32\t- `session_meta` writes four new session-log columns: `session-id`,\n33\t  `context-used`, `context-window`, `context-pct`.\n34\t- `project-trajectory/scripts/agent_common.py`: `write_session_log`'s\n35\t  header-key tuple carries the same four keys; `regenerate_index` gained a\n36\t  generated `Ctx %` column in `docs/iteration_index.md`.\n37\t- `docs/agents.toml`: `OPENCODE-GROK`'s `version` cell and `notes` prose\n38\t  corrected from \"4.5\" to \"4.6\" (the `model` cell and family comment were\n39\t  already fixed in a prior session) — the last of the stale grok slug.\n40\t- Tests: extended `test_session_meta_is_the_log_row_in_the_logs_own_column_order`\n41\t  for the four new keys; new coverage for `family_context_telemetry`\n42\t  (ANTHROPIC four-counter collision and ambiguous-match handling,\n43\t  ANTHROPIC with no usage at all, and the non-ANTHROPIC blank path) and for `write_session_log` /\n44\t  `regenerate_index` carrying the new columns through.\n45\t\n46\tNot in scope (WI-540, which `needs = [\"WI-535\"]`): session mint/resume, the\n47\tretention store, the `docs/process.toml [adjudicator]` table, and any\n48\tOPENAI/OPENCODE adapter.\n49\t\n50\t## Context\n51\t\n52\tStep 1 of the adjudicator session-retention plan's sequenced work (plan §5,\n53\tthe SpecRef anchor above): \"Telemetry first, dial off — session-id capture +\n54\toccupancy/window/pct columns per family; fix the stale\n55\t`opencode-go/grok-4.5` slug (install has grok-4.6). Independently useful: it\n56\tshows how full today's one-shot adjudications already get.\" OI-69 (the five\n57\towner rulings step 2 asked for) is already RULED\n58\t(`docs/log.d/2026-08-30-owner-rulings-oi68-oi69.md`,\n59\t`docs/requirements/open-items.toml#OI-69`), and its own recommendation says\n60\tthis telemetry row is unblocked and lands with the dial off — WI-540 (the\n61\tretention layer proper, `adjudicator_session.py` + the `[adjudicator]` table)\n62\t`needs = [\"WI-535\"]` and starts after this row.\n63\t\n64\tScope is telemetry only: no mint, no resume argv, no session store, no\n65\t`docs/process.toml [adjudicator]` table (WI-540's job). What this row adds is\n66\twhat today's plain one-shot call from each family already reports about its\n67\town session and context, captured into the existing session-log columns\n68\t(plan §3.2/§3.3): ANTHROPIC's stream-json result already carries\n69\t`session_id` on every call, and its `usage`/`modelUsage` fields already carry\n70\tenough to compute occupancy, window and percent without any adapter change.\n71\tOPENAI (codex) and OPENCODE do not emit any of this from their shipped\n72\tone-shot templates (no `--json`/`--format json`), so their columns read\n73\tblank until WI-540's per-family adapter lands — consistent with how `tokens`,\n74\t`cost-usd` etc. already read blank for those families today.\n75\t\n76\tThe stale grok slug: `docs/agents.toml`'s `OPENCODE-GROK` row had its `model`\n77\tcell already corrected to `opencode-go/grok-4.6` and its family-comment prose\n78\tin a prior session (`9ab30d64`, 2026-08-30), but the row's own `version` cell\n79\tand `notes` prose still read \"4.5\" — the remainder of that same staleness.\n80\t\n81\tIndependent review found that the first implementation identified the\n82\tsession's `modelUsage` entry by input/output alone even though cache-read and\n83\tcache-creation contribute to occupancy. The rework therefore makes the same\n84\tfour-counter tuple the identity predicate as well as the occupancy source and\n85\trequires exactly one match; this is the scoped correction to the shipped row.\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2101454a-ae43-4221-8363-b68a364a7b97","uuid":"0febd1ef-2eb4-4cf4-b1b5-a07ebac78a4f","timestamp":"2026-08-31T02:14:22.046Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template-drive\\wi-535-adjudicator-telemetry-first\\docs\\archive\\work\\complete\\WI-535-adjudicator-telemetry-first.md","content":"+++\nid = \"WI-535\"\ntitle = \"Adjudicator telemetry first, dial off: session id and occupancy / window / percent per family; the stale grok slug\"\nspecref = \"\"\nworkstream = \"process\"\nsr_refs = []\nneeds = []\nbuildtier = \"quick\"\nsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\npriority = 2\n+++\n\n## Deliverable\n\nTelemetry-first step of the adjudicator session-retention plan (plan §5 step\n1), landed with the retention dial off — no mint, no resume argv, no session\nstore, no `[adjudicator]` table (WI-540's job):\n\n- `project-trajectory/scripts/agent_loop.py`: new `family_context_telemetry(family, data)`\n  reads session id and context occupancy/window/percent straight off the\n  process's own JSON result, per family. ANTHROPIC's stream-json result\n  already carries `session_id` on every call; occupancy sums the same four\n  `usage` counters `session_meta` already partially reads\n  (input + cache-read + cache-creation + output); window is picked only from\n  the unique `modelUsage` entry whose own four counters match those same\n  top-level totals, so a subagent with colliding input/output but different\n  cache usage is never mistaken for the session — left blank when a full\n  match is absent or ambiguous, per the plan's \"never guessed\" rule. OPENAI/OPENCODE\n  return blank: their shipped one-shot templates carry no\n  `--json`/`--format json`, so there is nothing to parse until WI-540's\n  per-family adapter lands.\n- `session_meta` writes four new session-log columns: `session-id`,\n  `context-used`, `context-window`, `context-pct`.\n- `project-trajectory/scripts/agent_common.py`: `write_session_log`'s\n  header-key tuple carries the same four keys; `regenerate_index` gained a\n  generated `Ctx %` column in `docs/iteration_index.md`.\n- `docs/agents.toml`: `OPENCODE-GROK`'s `version` cell and `notes` prose\n  corrected from \"4.5\" to \"4.6\" (the `model` cell and family comment were\n  already fixed in a prior session) — the last of the stale grok slug.\n- Tests: extended `test_session_meta_is_the_log_row_in_the_logs_own_column_order`\n  for the four new keys; new coverage for `family_context_telemetry`\n  (ANTHROPIC four-counter collision and ambiguous-match handling,\n  ANTHROPIC with no usage at all, and the non-ANTHROPIC blank path) and for `write_session_log` /\n  `regenerate_index` carrying the new columns through.\n\nNot in scope (WI-540, which `needs = [\"WI-535\"]`): session mint/resume, the\nretention store, the `docs/process.toml [adjudicator]` table, and any\nOPENAI/OPENCODE adapter.\n\n## Context\n\nStep 1 of the adjudicator session-retention plan's sequenced work (plan §5,\nthe SpecRef anchor above): \"Telemetry first, dial off — session-id capture +\noccupancy/window/pct columns per family; fix the stale\n`opencode-go/grok-4.5` slug (install has grok-4.6). Independently useful: it\nshows how full today's one-shot adjudications already get.\" OI-69 (the five\nowner rulings step 2 asked for) is already RULED\n(`docs/log.d/2026-08-30-owner-rulings-oi68-oi69.md`,\n`docs/requirements/open-items.toml#OI-69`), and its own recommendation says\nthis telemetry row is unblocked and lands with the dial off — WI-540 (the\nretention layer proper, `adjudicator_session.py` + the `[adjudicator]` table)\n`needs = [\"WI-535\"]` and starts after this row.\n\nScope is telemetry only: no mint, no resume argv, no session store, no\n`docs/process.toml [adjudicator]` table (WI-540's job). What this row adds is\nwhat today's plain one-shot call from each family already reports about its\nown session and context, captured into the existing session-log columns\n(plan §3.2/§3.3): ANTHROPIC's stream-json result already carries\n`session_id` on every call, and its `usage`/`modelUsage` fields already carry\nenough to compute occupancy, window and percent without any adapter change.\nOPENAI (codex) and OPENCODE do not emit any of this from their shipped\none-shot templates (no `--json`/`--format json`), so their columns read\nblank until WI-540's per-family adapter lands — consistent with how `tokens`,\n`cost-usd` etc. already read blank for those families today.\n\nThe stale grok slug: `docs/agents.toml`'s `OPENCODE-GROK` row had its `model`\ncell already corrected to `opencode-go/grok-4.6` and its family-comment prose\nin a prior session (`9ab30d64`, 2026-08-30), but the row's own `version` cell\nand `notes` prose still read \"4.5\" — the remainder of that same staleness.\n\nIndependent review found that the first implementation identified the\nsession's `modelUsage` entry by input/output alone even though cache-read and\ncache-creation contribute to occupancy. The rework therefore makes the same\nfour-counter tuple the identity predicate as well as the occupancy source and\nrequires exactly one match; this is the scoped correction to the shipped row.\n","numLines":86,"startLine":1,"totalLines":86}}}
